From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GDmio <zhalin66@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:53:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/31] BlueOS: SystemUI: Halo lock screen

- Halo is the default clock (lockscreen_clock_id_fallback).
- The wallpaper under the clock and under the date is sampled (region sampling,
  unreleased upstream), so text is dark on a light wallpaper even in the dark
  theme; a clock color picked by the user is used in a tone that reads there.
- One-line (small) clock: the halo goes over the minutes, like over "OS" in
  the logo; the stacked large clock keeps it on top.
- Halos never fly away: when the clock switches size the halo fades well
  before the digits (it disappears and appears instead of moving), and on
  unlock it disappears in the first quarter of the transition.
- Greeting to Sensei by the time of day above the date, and a "what's next"
  card with the next calendar event (within 12 h, SystemUI gets READ_CALENDAR)
  and the next alarm; both fade out on AOD.

Change-Id: I53889ed0e900edc22976e2f26b878464999018e7
